{
  "schema": 1,
  "about": "What RuneLite's detectors must make of real game signals (Stage 4), and what the app must make of those events. The plugin runs its detectors over each case's signals, in order, and expects exactly the case's events. The app classifies each event against a run where it is new and expects its verdict. Written by hand, unlike the bundles; the manifest lists it so the plugin copies it at a pinned commit.",
  "signals": {
    "chat": "A chat message as RuneLite's ChatMessage carries it: its type and its text with colour tags.",
    "popup": "The game's notification popup: its title and main text as the game sets them.",
    "levels": "Real skill levels read at login or when the plugin starts: the baseline.",
    "level": "A skill's real level after a StatChanged.",
    "quests": "Every quest the game says is finished, by RuneLite's quest name. The first reading is the baseline.",
    "varbits": "A full reading of the varbits the detectors read, by id: the diary tiers (the baseline) and the collection log's notification setting (11959).",
    "varbit": "One varbit's new value.",
    "slayer": "The Slayer task as the game's variables give it: the task's name from the game's task table, the amount left and the amount assigned, the master's value, the task streak for that master, and whether it's a boss task (bossTask, false when absent)."
  },
  "events": "Each event names its type, label, confidence, detector and version, and evidence exactly. The app's verdict is READY or NEEDS_CONFIRMATION; firstCandidate is the choice a review starts on; a pet has none, as RuneLite can't tell which pet it is and the player picks it.",
  "run": "The app classifies against a Vanilla run for Iron Example with every skill unlocked at level 1 and every boss unlocked, plus the case's given unlocks.",
